**BREAKING CHANGES:**
- Frontend `ProjectInfo` object that is returned from the backend needs to change to accommodate JSON values (members,  tempDbDetails) - it might break depending if you have any values currently in the db as they have been saved into DB as strings not JSONs. See below structures and more details
- Also the tempDbDetails need to change as the Browse hub is using some of the info (name, type), but we don't want to show the rest of the info - question is, what is even the point of showing the database name and type to in browse hub, it's not like the people would care about that when they apply for analysis as they relay on the Archetypes. So maybe remove that from the Browse Hub project details???


**Changes:**
- added GET `/project/:projectId/public` endpoint for Browse Hub project details
- added GET `/archetype/:projectId/published` endpoint for Browse Hub project published archetypes (returns archetype without column nodes-edges and permissions)
- added better error handling to project and archetype service
- fixed typos in DTO's


Here's more details of the breaking changes:

```ts

export interface ConnectionInfo {
  requestId?: string;
  orgAdminEmail?: string;
  tempDbDetails?: {
    name: string;
    type: string;
    url?: string;
    username?: string;
    password?: string;
  };
  additionalInfo?: string;
}

export interface Member {
  email?: string;
  role?: string;
  name?: string;
}

export interface ProjectInfo {
  projectId?: string;
  status?: 'PENDING' | 'CRAWLING' | 'READY' | 'ERROR' | 'MAPPED';
  customId?: string;
  ownerId: string;
  name: string;
  lead: string;
  university: string;
  faculty: string;
  ethicsId: string;
  description: string;
  startDate: Date;
  endDate: Date;
  members: Member[];
  participantsNum: string;
  lastModified?: Date;
  dbKeywords?: string[];
  connection: ConnectionInfo;
}
```

This also links to you PR where you used inline modifications with member and tempDbDetails:

```ts
const memberData = JSON.stringify(response.data.members);
  response.data.members = memberData;

  const dbData = JSON.parse(response.data.connection.tempDbDetails);
  response.data.connection.tempDbDetails = dbData;
```
`The problem was that they where stored in the DB as string not JSON Value`

I've started a branch with frontend changes that need to happen, but didn't manage to fix all the errors and didn't want to change the same files you will be changes. For reference - https://github.com/Epsilon-Data/frontend/tree/test-browse-hub-endpoints

